<!--
    What an app may use of the SDK's resources: only the view ids for UI tests
    (README, "UI tests"). Everything else (strings, styles, drawables, colors,
    animations, the internal view tags) is private: Android Studio does not
    offer it, and lint warns an app that uses it or defines a resource of the
    same name (PrivateResource), so an app neither builds on texts that change
    nor overrides the SDK's look by accident. A new id for UI tests goes into
    dw_ids.xml, the README's table and this file.
-->
